From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Subject: mod-lr-logrotate: don't call back into DeviceInfo on stop

On stop, the module destructor runs "logrotate -f" through system()
and waits for it. The lastaction script of the syslog entries,
logrotate_add.sh, calls DeviceInfo.UpdateLogRotate() with ba-cli,
which deviceinfo-manager serves itself. On glibc, dlclose() unloads
the module during the stop, while the bus is still up, so the
daemon and ba-cli wait for each other until procd sends SIGKILL:

  procd: Instance deviceinfo-manager::deviceinfo-manager pid 4681 not stopped on SIGTERM, sending SIGKILL instead

On musl dlclose() does nothing, the destructor runs at exit and the
call fails fast, so the bug stays hidden there.

Set LOGROTATE_DM_STOPPING while the destructor runs logrotate, and
make logrotate_add.sh return early when it is set. The daemon stops
anyway, so the skipped update loses nothing.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
diff -ruN a/mod-lr-logrotate/src/mod-lr-logrotate.c b/mod-lr-logrotate/src/mod-lr-logrotate.c
--- a/mod-lr-logrotate/src/mod-lr-logrotate.c
+++ b/mod-lr-logrotate/src/mod-lr-logrotate.c
@@ -270,7 +270,14 @@
     SAH_TRACEZ_IN(ME);
     SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "Stopping mod-lr-logrotate");
 
+    /*
+     * The destructor can run while the plug-in stops (dlclose), with this
+     * process blocked in system(). A logrotate script that calls back into
+     * DeviceInfo over the bus would then wait forever: tell it not to.
+     */
+    setenv("LOGROTATE_DM_STOPPING", "1", 1);
     rotate_logs();
+    unsetenv("LOGROTATE_DM_STOPPING");
 
     logrotate_list_foreach(remove_entry);
     logrotate_list_clean();
diff -ruN a/scripts/logrotate_add.sh b/scripts/logrotate_add.sh
--- a/scripts/logrotate_add.sh
+++ b/scripts/logrotate_add.sh
@@ -7,6 +7,12 @@
     exit 22
 fi
 
+# Run from mod-lr-logrotate while deviceinfo-manager stops: a call into
+# DeviceInfo would block, because the daemon waits for logrotate.
+if [ -n "$LOGROTATE_DM_STOPPING" ]; then
+    exit 0
+fi
+
 FILENAME_PATH=$1  # e.g: /var/log/messages
 ALIAS=$2          # e.g: cpe-LogRotate-1
 
